1
00:00:47,422 --> 00:00:48,465
What's this?

2
00:00:48,548 --> 00:00:49,966
You're making a move on your own?

3
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:52,510
- And who were you talking to?
- My asset.

4
00:00:52,594 --> 00:00:53,845
And since when did you have an asset?

5
00:00:53,928 --> 00:00:56,097
Just leave me alone, Alex.
I know what I'm doing.

6
00:00:56,723 --> 00:00:58,683
What matters is I can reach him
through the landline,

7
00:00:58,767 --> 00:01:00,560
and he gives me vital information.

8
00:01:02,437 --> 00:01:04,731
Rahmboy, son, go with Chiara,

9
00:01:04,814 --> 00:01:07,067
so the Castellanis can see you.

10
00:01:12,822 --> 00:01:15,742
That's why the Moravianos
don't take you seriously.

11
00:01:17,786 --> 00:01:19,079
Rahmboy, you're coming with me.

12
00:01:24,626 --> 00:01:28,254
Are you telling me, Mikoy,
that you're getting all of this

13
00:01:28,338 --> 00:01:29,756
from your secret asset?

14
00:01:29,839 --> 00:01:31,466
- Yes, sir.
- How do you know

15
00:01:31,549 --> 00:01:33,176
that your intel is legit?

16
00:01:33,259 --> 00:01:35,011
I'm sorry, my asset is top secret.

17
00:01:35,094 --> 00:01:36,763
Maybe in time, you'll understand why.

18
00:01:38,181 --> 00:01:40,809
She wants every move she makes
to be a statement.

19
00:01:40,892 --> 00:01:43,269
She needs to prove through her actions

20
00:01:48,566 --> 00:01:49,943
<i>We're on the same side.</i>

21
00:01:50,026 --> 00:01:51,361
<i>You can count on me, Chiara.</i>

22
00:01:53,196 --> 00:01:54,989
But I want you to remember this too.

23
00:02:07,544 --> 00:02:11,089
Let's say Mikoy's intel is valid.

24
00:02:11,673 --> 00:02:14,509
The next question is, is it actionable?

25
00:02:15,802 --> 00:02:16,678
Exactly.

26
00:02:17,554 --> 00:02:19,848
Do you think Sir Norberto will agree?

27
00:02:19,931 --> 00:02:20,974
Didn't he

28
00:02:21,057 --> 00:02:22,725
say it himself

29
00:02:22,809 --> 00:02:24,435
that this is our golden window?

30
00:02:24,519 --> 00:02:27,856
If we don't act now
and go to Italy right away,

31
00:02:27,939 --> 00:02:30,066
we'll end up wasting the intel we have.

32
00:02:30,150 --> 00:02:30,984
Exactly.

33
00:02:31,568 --> 00:02:34,821
Our golden window might just turn
into a goodbye window.

34
00:02:36,614 --> 00:02:39,200
It is a golden window,
theoretically speaking.

35
00:02:40,702 --> 00:02:41,870
But us,

36
00:02:41,953 --> 00:02:44,622
who is just a small intelligence agency
from the Philippines

37
00:02:44,706 --> 00:02:47,458
who's already short on budget,

38
00:02:47,542 --> 00:02:48,960
what guarantee do we have

39
00:02:49,043 --> 00:02:51,796
that this mission will be successful?

40
00:02:52,338 --> 00:02:54,591
What guarantee do we have

41
00:02:54,674 --> 00:02:57,677
that we'll all make it back alive?

42
00:02:58,928 --> 00:03:00,722
Isn't that what every mission is like?

43
00:03:01,431 --> 00:03:03,433
There's always a risk involved.

44
00:03:04,100 --> 00:03:06,102
Half our lives are on the line.

45
00:03:07,896 --> 00:03:08,730
But it's okay.

46
00:03:08,813 --> 00:03:11,774
If you don't want to come with me,
that's okay. I understand.

47
00:03:12,901 --> 00:03:14,903
Even just some moral support
would be nice.

48
00:03:14,986 --> 00:03:15,945
That'll do.

49
00:03:16,029 --> 00:03:17,488
As for you, Mikoy,

50
00:03:17,572 --> 00:03:18,948
I have complete faith in you.

51
00:03:19,032 --> 00:03:20,366
Weren't you the one who taught me

52
00:03:20,450 --> 00:03:22,535
how to be a good person,

53
00:03:22,619 --> 00:03:24,120
how to do the right thing?

54
00:03:24,203 --> 00:03:25,204
Right?

55
00:03:25,830 --> 00:03:26,915
Mikoy.

56
00:03:32,462 --> 00:03:34,547
this isn't an ordinary mission.

57
00:03:35,215 --> 00:03:36,883
It's extremely dangerous.

58
00:03:38,134 --> 00:03:39,010
That's true.

59
00:03:40,053 --> 00:03:41,387
If you think about it,

60
00:03:41,471 --> 00:03:43,264
we're going to a place

61
00:03:43,348 --> 00:03:47,435
where the most powerful mafia
are gathering for a meeting.

62
00:03:48,186 --> 00:03:50,271
We need to calculate every move we make.

63
00:03:51,272 --> 00:03:53,358
One mistake there,

64
00:03:54,400 --> 00:03:55,652
and we're all dead.

65
00:04:22,136 --> 00:04:25,014
<i>I cannot let my mission fail.</i>

66
00:05:01,634 --> 00:05:05,054
A black-and-white romcom
is really your RRL for your research?

67
00:05:06,556 --> 00:05:08,016
A romcom, of all things.

68
00:05:08,933 --> 00:05:10,810
It's a classic for a reason.

69
00:05:11,519 --> 00:05:13,313
No matter how many times you watch it,

70
00:05:14,230 --> 00:05:15,815
it's still enjoyable.

71
00:05:17,734 --> 00:05:19,861
Is it still enjoyable
if it doesn't have a happy ending?

72
00:05:19,944 --> 00:05:21,654
Oh, Mikoy.

73
00:05:21,738 --> 00:05:23,823
You really are
a classic hopeless romantic.

74
00:05:26,159 --> 00:05:29,871
You know, we'd be better off
talking about that over a few drinks.

75
00:05:48,306 --> 00:05:49,974
You're suddenly so quiet.

76
00:05:50,683 --> 00:05:52,435
You said earlier

77
00:05:52,518 --> 00:05:54,270
we'd talk about it over drinks.

78
00:05:58,357 --> 00:05:59,484
With or without alcohol,

79
00:05:59,567 --> 00:06:01,944
it's hard to talk
about this mission, Mikoy.

80
00:06:06,657 --> 00:06:08,951
Mikoy, Chiara is our target.

81
00:06:14,082 --> 00:06:15,041
Really?

82
00:06:16,084 --> 00:06:17,752
Has it really come to this?

83
00:06:18,795 --> 00:06:20,588
We're actually ready to kill her?

84
00:06:28,012 --> 00:06:29,972
That's just how the world works.

85
00:06:31,724 --> 00:06:34,143
Maybe this really is the ending
to our story.

86
00:06:36,187 --> 00:06:37,772
The person who used to be your ally,

87
00:06:38,564 --> 00:06:41,317
who stood beside you
as you built your dreams for the future,

88
00:06:43,069 --> 00:06:45,488
you have to face her
as if you never had a history together.

89
00:06:46,823 --> 00:06:48,533
Face her to make her pay.

90
00:06:49,534 --> 00:06:51,410
A life for a life.

91
00:06:59,127 --> 00:07:00,628
That's where you're wrong, Mikoy.

92
00:07:03,047 --> 00:07:04,590
No matter how you look at it, it's wrong.

93
00:07:04,674 --> 00:07:05,591
Why?

94
00:07:06,092 --> 00:07:07,885
Was it right when she killed my father?

95
00:07:14,308 --> 00:07:15,351
You said it yourself.

96
00:07:15,435 --> 00:07:17,103
Do it the right way.

97
00:07:17,770 --> 00:07:21,357
That's why I laid out my plan properly
to the agencies, didn't I?

98
00:07:23,359 --> 00:07:26,154
Even if we say the agency supports this,

99
00:07:26,654 --> 00:07:28,531
even if there's an official order,

100
00:07:29,866 --> 00:07:31,200
it's still wrong.

101
00:07:36,080 --> 00:07:37,915
Because, Mikoy, this isn't you.

102
00:07:39,792 --> 00:07:42,670
You're not the kind of person
who seeks revenge.

103
00:07:44,130 --> 00:07:46,799
And you're not
the kind of person who can kill.

104
00:07:47,592 --> 00:07:49,594
Especially not the person you love most.

105
00:07:59,187 --> 00:08:00,813
The person I used to love.

106
00:08:09,322 --> 00:08:11,657
Love doesn't just disappear.

107
00:08:13,659 --> 00:08:15,203
Maybe some things just changed.

108
00:08:16,829 --> 00:08:18,789
Maybe it gained some layers

109
00:08:19,540 --> 00:08:21,209
or lost some of its intensity.

110
00:08:26,631 --> 00:08:28,090
Is that you, Alex?

111
00:08:28,174 --> 00:08:30,301
You're a hopeless romantic after all.

112
00:08:31,302 --> 00:08:34,680
I remember all those warnings
you gave me about Chiara.

113
00:08:34,764 --> 00:08:36,182
You were so harsh back then.

114
00:08:39,727 --> 00:08:40,895
I was naive back then.

115
00:08:42,063 --> 00:08:44,065
I was blind to all those red flags.

116
00:08:45,608 --> 00:08:48,486
I always gave her
the benefit of the doubt.

117
00:08:50,363 --> 00:08:52,490
Apparently, that's what happens
when you're a romantic.

118
00:08:53,991 --> 00:08:55,451
You're always hopeful.

119
00:08:58,329 --> 00:08:59,705
Hopeful that

120
00:09:01,499 --> 00:09:03,000
things might still change.

121
00:09:05,336 --> 00:09:06,629
Hopeful that…

122
00:09:09,340 --> 00:09:11,133
there's still a tomorrow
to look forward to.

123
00:09:12,969 --> 00:09:15,263
Maybe that's why it bothers me
to see you like this.

124
00:09:19,976 --> 00:09:21,269
You're just not used to it.

125
00:09:22,937 --> 00:09:24,313
Everyone changes.

126
00:09:28,276 --> 00:09:30,444
I hope this mission can change you back.

127
00:09:33,489 --> 00:09:34,949
As much as my brain can't imagine

128
00:09:35,032 --> 00:09:37,535
you and Chiara getting back together,
but you know,

129
00:09:38,411 --> 00:09:39,787
in my heart…

130
00:09:48,546 --> 00:09:51,215
Because I know
you're just caught in a situation

131
00:09:52,550 --> 00:09:54,760
by the past you share
that you can't escape.

132
00:10:00,641 --> 00:10:01,892
You know,

133
00:10:03,603 --> 00:10:05,438
I think you're drunk already, Alex.

134
00:10:07,064 --> 00:10:08,399
That's enough.

135
00:10:10,651 --> 00:10:12,028
Chiara and I are over,

136
00:10:12,903 --> 00:10:14,822
and there's nothing left to go back to.

137
00:10:16,574 --> 00:10:18,326
We've both chosen our own lives.

138
00:10:18,409 --> 00:10:20,077
For now, this is mine,

139
00:10:20,161 --> 00:10:21,829
to finish this mission.

140
00:10:21,912 --> 00:10:23,164
That's it.

141
00:10:26,542 --> 00:10:27,918
If that's the case…

142
00:10:29,962 --> 00:10:32,632
then I hope the old Mikoy I knew
comes back.

143
00:10:37,136 --> 00:10:38,471
Even just that.

144
00:10:51,776 --> 00:10:53,986
let's just wait and see how this ends.

145
00:11:11,504 --> 00:11:12,671
Mom.

146
00:11:12,755 --> 00:11:15,091
You've been staring
into space for a while now.

147
00:11:15,174 --> 00:11:17,593
Come eat. The food's getting cold.

148
00:11:20,429 --> 00:11:22,681
I was just thinking about your brother.

149
00:11:23,766 --> 00:11:25,684
I wonder how he's doing over there.

150
00:11:26,560 --> 00:11:28,479
He's always in Manila now,

151
00:11:28,562 --> 00:11:30,147
and he always seems so busy.

152
00:11:30,856 --> 00:11:32,858
I wonder what he's busy with now.

153
00:11:35,027 --> 00:11:37,446
He said he's okay, Mom.

154
00:11:38,072 --> 00:11:39,907
But we know him so well.

155
00:11:39,990 --> 00:11:43,160
He wouldn't admit it
if he was having a hard time.

156
00:11:43,244 --> 00:11:46,038
He'll show that he can handle it,

157
00:11:46,122 --> 00:11:47,748
but deep down,

158
00:11:47,832 --> 00:11:49,458
he's struggling too.

159
00:11:52,002 --> 00:11:53,796
That's just how your brother is.

160
00:11:54,880 --> 00:11:56,090
But you know,

161
00:11:57,133 --> 00:11:59,718
no matter how heavy the burden is,

162
00:12:00,302 --> 00:12:02,972
I'm sure he'll get through all of it.

163
00:12:04,265 --> 00:12:05,850
You're right, Mom.

164
00:12:06,851 --> 00:12:08,185
But you know, Mom,

165
00:12:08,853 --> 00:12:12,690
if he keeps dealing
with all his problems on his own,

166
00:12:12,773 --> 00:12:15,568
why don't we show him
that we're here for him,

167
00:12:15,651 --> 00:12:16,819
that we support him,

168
00:12:16,902 --> 00:12:18,946
that we're his number one support system?

169
00:12:19,947 --> 00:12:20,781
Right?

170
00:12:20,865 --> 00:12:22,658
I agree with you, son.

171
00:12:25,244 --> 00:12:26,328
I have an idea.

172
00:12:32,710 --> 00:12:34,503
Hello, Captain Pepe.

173
00:12:35,004 --> 00:12:36,964
I was hoping to ask you a favor.

174
00:13:03,157 --> 00:13:04,867
It's so nice here!

175
00:13:07,578 --> 00:13:08,454
It's so cold here.

176
00:13:08,537 --> 00:13:09,580
It's so soft.

177
00:13:10,372 --> 00:13:11,499
Air-conditioning!

178
00:13:11,582 --> 00:13:13,334
- It's so soft!
- Leather!

179
00:13:13,417 --> 00:13:14,335
Air-conditioning!

180
00:13:14,418 --> 00:13:16,253
What is wrong with you guys?

181
00:13:16,337 --> 00:13:18,797
What's with all these surprises?

182
00:13:19,632 --> 00:13:23,135
Because you're never online anymore
on IG or Twitter.

183
00:13:23,219 --> 00:13:25,262
And you don't message in the group chat.

184
00:13:25,346 --> 00:13:27,765
You don't even view our My Days anymore.

185
00:13:27,848 --> 00:13:30,267
Don't you know they expire after 24 hours?

186
00:13:30,351 --> 00:13:31,685
Seriously!

187
00:13:31,769 --> 00:13:35,064
I can't even tell if you're my friends
or my clingy girlfriends!

188
00:13:36,106 --> 00:13:37,358
Of course, Mikoy.

189
00:13:37,441 --> 00:13:39,360
We're a team. We're like the GILAS, right?

190
00:13:39,443 --> 00:13:40,528
When there's Mikoy…

191
00:13:40,611 --> 00:13:42,488
There's the Kolokoys!

192
00:13:43,072 --> 00:13:44,490
Heart!

193
00:13:44,573 --> 00:13:47,034
Mikoy, we miss you!

194
00:13:47,117 --> 00:13:47,952
Exactly.

195
00:13:51,747 --> 00:13:53,040
See?

196
00:13:53,123 --> 00:13:57,086
Even me, Mikoy, you take forever to reply.

197
00:13:57,169 --> 00:13:58,420
Even me, son.

198
00:13:58,504 --> 00:14:00,297
You don't answer my calls.

199
00:14:00,381 --> 00:14:01,215
See?

200
00:14:01,298 --> 00:14:02,633
See? See?

201
00:14:03,676 --> 00:14:05,094
I'm sorry, everyone.

202
00:14:05,719 --> 00:14:06,971
I've just been really busy.

203
00:14:07,054 --> 00:14:08,973
I've had a lot to take care of.

204
00:14:09,056 --> 00:14:11,225
What are you so busy with?

205
00:14:15,062 --> 00:14:16,605
It's a secret for now, Mom.

206
00:14:17,273 --> 00:14:19,400
Oh, here we go again, son.

207
00:14:19,483 --> 00:14:21,068
Another secret.

208
00:14:21,151 --> 00:14:22,152
Another secret.

209
00:14:22,236 --> 00:14:24,488
Is there something we should
be worried about again, bro?

210
00:14:25,406 --> 00:14:27,741
No! I'm okay, okay?

211
00:14:27,825 --> 00:14:29,869
Guys, I'm really okay.

212
00:14:29,952 --> 00:14:31,787
I'm more than alright, actually.

213
00:14:31,871 --> 00:14:32,955
Are you sure?

214
00:14:33,038 --> 00:14:34,999
Yeah, but

215
00:14:35,082 --> 00:14:36,500
when the time is right,

216
00:14:36,584 --> 00:14:37,710
you'll all find out.

217
00:14:40,004 --> 00:14:42,006
For now, how about

218
00:14:42,756 --> 00:14:43,757
some ramyeon?

219
00:14:44,466 --> 00:14:45,301
Me!

220
00:14:45,384 --> 00:14:46,844
There's a good place nearby.

221
00:14:49,013 --> 00:14:50,764
- Okay!
- Does it come with soup?

222
00:14:50,848 --> 00:14:52,433
- Of course!
- No vegetables, right?

223
00:14:52,516 --> 00:14:54,476
Everything's for you guys!

224
00:14:54,560 --> 00:14:55,477
- Does it have soup?
- Of course!

225
00:14:55,561 --> 00:14:57,062
No vegetables, right? No vegetables?

226
00:14:59,148 --> 00:15:02,610
Son, isn't it nice
that the weather's so good today?

227
00:15:02,693 --> 00:15:03,694
The sun's out.

228
00:15:03,777 --> 00:15:05,237
Here in Manila,

229
00:15:05,321 --> 00:15:08,240
just a little rain and it floods!

230
00:15:09,158 --> 00:15:11,285
It's the same in some provinces, Mom.

231
00:15:11,368 --> 00:15:13,162
Climate change

232
00:15:13,245 --> 00:15:15,539
and all that corruption
are really a bad combo.

233
00:15:15,623 --> 00:15:16,707
You said it!

234
00:15:16,790 --> 00:15:18,584
And people who just throw
their trash everywhere!

235
00:15:18,667 --> 00:15:19,877
You know what needs to happen?

236
00:15:19,960 --> 00:15:22,546
Those officials need
to be held accountable,

237
00:15:22,630 --> 00:15:25,174
and those corrupt people
need to go to jail!

238
00:15:25,257 --> 00:15:26,175
- Exactly!
- Exactly!

239
00:15:26,258 --> 00:15:28,135
Anyone involved with them
should go to jail too!

240
00:15:28,218 --> 00:15:29,678
- Absolutely!
- Exactly!

241
00:15:30,179 --> 00:15:31,597
Even my pancit is overflowing,

242
00:15:31,680 --> 00:15:33,599
drowning in soup!

243
00:15:33,682 --> 00:15:35,017
This is so good!

244
00:15:35,684 --> 00:15:36,769
Wait a minute, son.

245
00:15:36,852 --> 00:15:39,355
Do I mix in this seasoning now?

246
00:15:40,814 --> 00:15:41,774
Oh, wait!

247
00:16:04,129 --> 00:16:05,631
Just relax, Chiara!

248
00:16:06,256 --> 00:16:09,551
It's instant cooking.
It'll be ready in a bit!

249
00:16:09,635 --> 00:16:10,678
Oh, you.

250
00:16:10,761 --> 00:16:12,471
Sweetheart, what are you doing?

251
00:16:12,554 --> 00:16:15,516
They say if you lift the noodles a little

252
00:16:16,892 --> 00:16:18,519
it lets air in,

253
00:16:18,602 --> 00:16:20,396
and it'll make the noodles firmer.

254
00:16:21,855 --> 00:16:22,982
Really?

255
00:16:23,482 --> 00:16:24,525
It seems like the same thing to me.

256
00:16:24,608 --> 00:16:26,026
They're going to cook anyway!

257
00:16:40,624 --> 00:16:41,667
Nice!

258
00:16:42,167 --> 00:16:43,377
You're really good, sweetheart!

259
00:16:43,460 --> 00:16:44,670
Look!

260
00:16:44,753 --> 00:16:46,505
The noodles are cooked perfectly!

261
00:16:46,588 --> 00:16:49,717
And it looks like
the seasoning stuck better!

262
00:17:02,855 --> 00:17:04,189
So, Mikoy?

263
00:17:05,065 --> 00:17:06,900
How was your flashback?

264
00:17:17,828 --> 00:17:19,580
Wasn't it such a happy time back then,

265
00:17:20,164 --> 00:17:21,623
when you two were still okay?

266
00:17:24,710 --> 00:17:26,879
It's hard when you're trying to move on

267
00:17:26,962 --> 00:17:29,089
and happy memories
suddenly come flooding back.

268
00:17:30,758 --> 00:17:32,551
Will you two stop it? Stop!

269
00:17:32,634 --> 00:17:34,762
Seriously, just leave
Brother Mikoy alone for now.

270
00:17:34,845 --> 00:17:37,514
Everyone who's been heartbroken
and is trying to move on

271
00:17:37,598 --> 00:17:40,309
has to go through it.
You can't rush the process.

272
00:17:42,770 --> 00:17:44,438
You're one to talk about rushing.

273
00:17:45,939 --> 00:17:47,524
You all, really.

274
00:17:47,608 --> 00:17:48,984
Eat up.

275
00:17:49,068 --> 00:17:50,277
It's still hot.

276
00:17:51,320 --> 00:17:52,404
Bro Mikoy.

277
00:17:53,447 --> 00:17:55,240
What stage are you at now?

278
00:17:58,410 --> 00:17:59,787
- Hangry stage?
- I'm starving.

279
00:17:59,870 --> 00:18:01,914
Then eat it already.

280
00:18:01,997 --> 00:18:02,998
There you go.

281
00:18:03,082 --> 00:18:04,124
I'm going to eat it.

282
00:18:05,584 --> 00:18:06,794
Come on, Mom. Eat up.

283
00:18:36,573 --> 00:18:37,950
What's wrong, dear?

284
00:18:40,202 --> 00:18:41,787
Do you miss Mikoy?

285
00:18:43,330 --> 00:18:44,331
Or

286
00:18:45,082 --> 00:18:47,960
do you miss the Philippines?

287
00:18:53,590 --> 00:18:55,300
Have some ramyeon first.

288
00:18:55,384 --> 00:18:58,929
Maybe it'll help you miss
the Philippines a little less.

289
00:19:01,181 --> 00:19:02,891
That's Korean noodles.

290
00:19:04,351 --> 00:19:05,644
Exactly.

291
00:19:06,436 --> 00:19:08,772
But it's really popular
in the Philippines.

292
00:19:09,439 --> 00:19:11,024
You know Filipinos.

293
00:19:11,108 --> 00:19:13,527
We never want to miss out on a trend.

294
00:19:16,905 --> 00:19:17,990
Dear.

295
00:19:18,073 --> 00:19:19,992
I understand what you're going through.

296
00:19:21,034 --> 00:19:23,287
I know this isn't easy for you.

297
00:19:23,370 --> 00:19:25,038
But we're almost there.

298
00:19:25,873 --> 00:19:27,374
Just hang in there a little longer.

299
00:19:28,542 --> 00:19:32,296
We'll sort out our problems
with the Castellanis.

300
00:19:33,297 --> 00:19:36,049
We'll all be able to breathe easier.

301
00:19:39,303 --> 00:19:41,805
That sounds impossible, Mama Yaya.

302
00:19:44,266 --> 00:19:48,228
In the mafia life, there's always
one problem after another,

303
00:19:48,312 --> 00:19:50,063
big or small.

304
00:19:50,939 --> 00:19:53,859
Even if we manage
to settle things with the Castellanis,

305
00:19:54,443 --> 00:19:56,653
I'm sure there'll be another one

306
00:19:56,737 --> 00:19:59,656
that'll challenge my leadership
of the Concordat.

307
00:20:01,700 --> 00:20:02,910
Look at me.

308
00:20:04,578 --> 00:20:08,498
La Morte Bianca raised me and trained me.

309
00:20:08,582 --> 00:20:09,708
But

310
00:20:10,751 --> 00:20:13,212
I still managed to stand up against her.

311
00:20:16,673 --> 00:20:18,133
I know, dear.

312
00:20:20,427 --> 00:20:22,012
That's why I'm here,

313
00:20:22,596 --> 00:20:24,473
always supporting you.

314
00:20:26,391 --> 00:20:28,477
Whatever you need,

315
00:20:28,560 --> 00:20:31,480
I'm ready to give it to you.

316
00:20:32,481 --> 00:20:33,982
For now,

317
00:20:34,066 --> 00:20:37,194
let's focus on the Castellanis.

318
00:20:38,362 --> 00:20:40,614
We know how cunning they are.

319
00:20:41,365 --> 00:20:43,075
So let's be careful.

320
00:20:50,958 --> 00:20:52,334
Mikoy.

321
00:20:53,210 --> 00:20:55,295
Tell me the truth.

322
00:20:56,546 --> 00:20:58,006
How are you?

323
00:20:58,590 --> 00:21:01,343
What have you been so busy with, son?

324
00:21:02,302 --> 00:21:03,512
And hold on.

325
00:21:03,595 --> 00:21:06,974
Don't give me some showbiz-style answer
and dodge the question.

326
00:21:07,516 --> 00:21:10,185
You can't just keep denying everything.

327
00:21:12,604 --> 00:21:15,065
I saw your gun earlier.

328
00:21:17,484 --> 00:21:18,944
I'm your mother.

329
00:21:19,027 --> 00:21:21,113
I deserve to know the truth.

330
00:21:27,703 --> 00:21:28,745
Mom,

331
00:21:29,830 --> 00:21:31,832
I've returned to active duty
with the agency.

332
00:21:35,794 --> 00:21:36,962
Since when?

333
00:21:38,005 --> 00:21:40,424
Is that why you're always here in Manila?

334
00:21:42,801 --> 00:21:44,136
Yes, Mom.

335
00:21:44,761 --> 00:21:46,430
And we have a mission.

336
00:21:54,229 --> 00:21:56,606
That's exactly what I was afraid of.

337
00:21:57,441 --> 00:22:00,235
Son, why did you have
to go back to that agency?

338
00:22:00,319 --> 00:22:03,572
You know there's no guarantee
with those missions.

339
00:22:07,075 --> 00:22:08,994
And after this mission,

340
00:22:09,077 --> 00:22:11,747
I'm really going back to a quiet,
simple life.

341
00:22:13,081 --> 00:22:14,166
I promise you that.

342
00:22:16,209 --> 00:22:17,627
Oh, son.

343
00:22:17,711 --> 00:22:20,464
Nothing good ever comes
from those missions!

344
00:22:20,547 --> 00:22:22,841
We just lost your father.

345
00:22:22,924 --> 00:22:26,428
You're all I have left. You and Angelito.

346
00:22:27,137 --> 00:22:28,638
I'll be careful, Mom.

347
00:22:30,515 --> 00:22:32,184
Mom, I'm really sorry.

348
00:22:32,809 --> 00:22:34,186
But I have to do this.

349
00:22:35,145 --> 00:22:37,397
Mom, I have to do this for Dad.

350
00:22:38,774 --> 00:22:40,067
For Mario?

351
00:22:40,901 --> 00:22:43,653
You're going to avenge your father?

352
00:22:44,780 --> 00:22:47,157
Revenge isn't the answer, son.

353
00:22:48,742 --> 00:22:51,495
Mom, I understand
that you're worried about me.

354
00:22:52,454 --> 00:22:53,455
But, Mom,

355
00:22:54,623 --> 00:22:56,249
I've already made my decision.

356
00:22:57,375 --> 00:22:59,544
And I'm fully committed to this mission.

357
00:23:01,004 --> 00:23:01,963
Mikoy.

358
00:23:02,923 --> 00:23:04,800
You know, I know

359
00:23:04,883 --> 00:23:07,219
how heavy the burden you're carrying is.

360
00:23:07,803 --> 00:23:09,387
Okay, I know that.

361
00:23:10,222 --> 00:23:14,017
But revenge isn't the answer, son.

362
00:23:14,101 --> 00:23:16,103
I know you.

363
00:23:17,729 --> 00:23:20,232
I know you have a good heart,

364
00:23:20,315 --> 00:23:23,443
and no matter how much anger
and pain you're going through,

365
00:23:23,527 --> 00:23:25,320
I know you'll make the right decision

366
00:23:25,403 --> 00:23:27,489
because you're a good person, son.

367
00:23:28,323 --> 00:23:30,242
You have a good heart.

368
00:23:46,091 --> 00:23:48,343
I called Malacañang last night.

369
00:23:48,426 --> 00:23:51,304
The Office of the President
had already given its approval.

370
00:24:05,610 --> 00:24:06,653
- Okay…
- Excuse me.

371
00:24:06,736 --> 00:24:07,988
- Excuse me.
- Hey!

372
00:24:33,847 --> 00:24:35,765
to everyone entering
and leaving the restaurant,

373
00:24:35,849 --> 00:24:38,310
and all I need is one shot
to take her out.

374
00:24:38,393 --> 00:24:39,644
And what will Mikoy do?

375
00:24:47,319 --> 00:24:50,822
They call us criminals, a syndicate.

376
00:24:50,906 --> 00:24:52,324
But aren't they the ones

377
00:24:53,241 --> 00:24:55,493
who are actually
the syndicate and criminals?

378
00:24:57,204 --> 00:25:00,207
I hope your wish is

379
00:25:00,290 --> 00:25:03,627
that everything goes smoothly tomorrow.

380
00:25:14,221 --> 00:25:16,389
I gave my heart to the wrong person.

381
00:25:16,473 --> 00:25:19,226
<i>But please, Mikoy,</i>
<i>continue believing in love.</i>

382
00:25:19,309 --> 00:25:21,353
Despite the world not believing in it.
